<p>Ukraine is sending drone-defense specialists and interceptor drones to the Middle East after the United States asked for help protecting U.S. military bases in Jordan, President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said in an interview published on March 9. Zelenskyy said the request came on Thursday and the Ukrainian team left the next day, with arrival expected soon. Zelenskyy framed the move—and related training offers—as a way to share Ukraine’s hard-won experience countering Russian drone and missile attacks. He argues that know-how can help partners shore up their defenses as Iranian-made drones play a major role both in the war against Ukraine and in regional conflicts. He also linked the cooperation to Kyiv’s push for continued Western air-defense support as Russia’s air attacks continue. Separately, Zelenskyy said he discussed expanding joint arms production with Dutch Prime Minister Rob Jetten during Jetten’s visit to Kyiv.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_lmI2nKMO5nrxq_K7ImPQBmMhu6EmyOo-G1teWP637WjBA8udEhoNEZG6MON2Q0vTSvmZenQUtJhwisR7BxJHjvGFpl96h-HqFxDfz2IJGWykNKkZjDH9KC8ufEVcLfrgpArXIaOfS56FJ6VHm2cbrBJT4971JYGIxDBECHQrt1rTAGKGk-Fsx-JTNJTecuMSbMl83GG' alt='Soldiers in Ukraine’s Donetsk region in December monitor the sky for Shahed drones, according to the image caption.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Reciprocal support: Zelenskyy pitched the outreach as a two-way street—“we help those who help us”—as Ukraine sends experts abroad while still relying on partner support against Russia.</li><li>Next-week site work: Zelenskyy said Ukraine’s drone experts would be on site in the Middle East “next week” to assess needs and advise on counter-drone defenses.</li><li>Supply risk: Kyiv worries that a prolonged Middle East war could further disrupt supplies of costly U.S. PAC-3 air-defense ammunition, which Ukraine says it is short of.</li><li>Tradeoff concern: The Guardian noted that rising demand for Ukraine’s drone-defense technology could open new defense partnerships, but it could also strain Ukraine’s own drone availability in a tight market.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Volodymyr Zelenskyy (Ukraine): He said Ukraine sent interceptor drones and experts after a U.S. request to help protect American bases in Jordan, and described Ukraine’s drone-defense experience as something it can share with partners. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/ukraine-sent-drone-experts-protect-us-bases-jordan-zelenskiy-tells-nyt'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Ukrainian government (via Zelenskyy): He presented the outreach as an exchange—offering drone expertise while seeking U.S. air-defence missiles—and said it was too early to share operational specifics before experts assess the situation on the ground. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/09/ukraine-war-briefing-drone-experts-will-be-in-middle-east-in-coming-days-says-zelenskyy'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Dutch government (Rob Jetten): During a visit to Kyiv, Jetten discussed expanding joint arms production with Ukraine, with Zelenskyy saying they reviewed investments and possible production volumes. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/zelenskiy-says-ukraine-has-unique-drone-experience-discusses-joint-production-with-dutch-pm'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>The New York Times (reporting): The paper highlighted Kyiv’s push to turn battlefield counter-drone know-how into help for partners as Iranian drones remain a central threat, describing Ukraine as offering both expertise and technology amid widening regional drone warfare. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/09/world/middleeast/ukraine-shahed-drone-middle-east.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/we-help-those-who-help-us-ukrainian-military-experts-head-to-west-asia-to-share-battlefield-lessons-13987528.html'>&#x27;We help those who help us&#x27;: Ukrainian military experts head to West Asia to share battlefield lessons</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/ukraine-sent-drone-experts-protect-us-bases-jordan-zelenskiy-tells-nyt'>Ukraine sent drone experts to protect US bases in Jordan, Zelenskiy tells NYT</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/zelenskiy-says-ukraine-has-unique-drone-experience-discusses-joint-production-with-dutch-pm'>Zelenskiy says Ukraine has unique drone experience, discusses joint production with Dutch PM</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/09/ukraine-war-briefing-drone-experts-will-be-in-middle-east-in-coming-days-says-zelenskyy'>Ukraine war briefing: drone experts will be in Middle East in coming days, says Zelenskyy</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/09/world/middleeast/ukraine-shahed-drone-middle-east.html'>Ukraine Sent Drone Experts to Protect U.S. Bases in Jordan, Zelensky Says</a> - nytimes.com</li></ul>